Everything under this directory is a Derivative Database of OpenStreetMap.

  (c) OpenStreetMap contributors, available under the Open Database License.
  https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright

The contents are extracted from the taginfo database dumps, which are
distributed under ODbL:

  https://taginfo.openstreetmap.org/download
  https://taginfo.openstreetmap.org/about

Two dumps of 2026-01-30 are used. taginfo-wiki.db supplies the descriptions,
the opening paragraphs, the related terms, the status and the geometry
applicability, all of which originate in pages of the OpenStreetMap Wiki.
taginfo-db.db supplies the worldwide usage counts, which are aggregated from
OpenStreetMap data itself. data/provenance.yaml records which tables were read
and which were deliberately skipped.

The extraction keeps the wording of the source: descriptions are copied
verbatim, and the opening paragraphs are the wiki text with templates and
markup resolved, split into sentences. src/formats.py assembles these fields
into sentences at load time; those sentences are likewise derived from OSM and
carry ODbL, as does any index or embedding built from them.

ODbL-1.0 section 4.2 permits redistribution to satisfy the notice requirement
by including either a copy of the licence or its URI. This file supplies the
URI above. The full text is at that address.

The MIT licence in the repository root covers the source code in src/ and does
not apply here.
